ve max-product metric. D002 is the total extended diameter; finite real diameters are used only after a finite scale bounds them. D003 retains the exact original covering infimum, countability, empty-member convention and supremum over positive scales; only the trailing incomplete word from the copied passage was removed. D004-D005 use the native gauge measure and native supremum definition of dimension: pinned Hausdorff.lean:535-552 and HausdorffDimension.lean:94-135 were read, and R001 proves the positive-exponent normalization bridge. D006-D008 define I,F,D without granting dimension or finiteness properties; finiteness of D is proved in N002 before subsequent real-exponent limits. D009 is the finite-open-subcover definition actually used in R002, not a compactness conclusion hidden in a definition. D010-D012 specify the measure, lower integral and indicators; no measurability of arbitrary covering sets is assumed. Construction guards were checked at R003/S001-S002 (q>0 and n≥1 before the small positive balls), R004/S002 (positive r_i before division and the ceiling), R005/S002 (nonempty bounded B before the real infimum/supremum), and R006/S001-S003 (finite c, finite nonnegative diameters, positive error denominators and Borel intervals before integration). All 13 M declarations have successful same-stage probes with pinned signatures and official-source readback: M001-M005 in the Hausdorff files; M006-M008 in Lebesgue Add/Basic; M009-M010 in Lebesgue Basic; M011 in OuterMeasure Basic; M012-M013 in Pow Continuity/Asymptotics. Their NL statements preserve native measurable/Borel, extended-metric, countability, almost-everywhere measurability, order and exponent premises. The initially guessed namespace for M013 failed and was replaced by the actually probed unnamespaced theorem. Ordered attempts to retrieve the cited Stein-Shakarchi book were unsuccessful and are preserved in the access records; that book is not an imported theorem root, and no inaccessible-primary assumption or unverified E is used. Principal tools are supplied by the verified native sources instead. The graph has 25 propositions and nine producers; all selected M and all eight N are in P's backward AND closure, while H001 is explicitly reported unused. R002-R009 follow every required phase of problem.md:49-167: bounded-dimension grid, singleton replacements, interval product covers with the factor 2(√2)^{q+1}, same-scale slicing with η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s), Tonelli, error removal and infimum, the s↑D limit, and the interval/isometric-fibre treatment of D=0 including n=0. No needed calculation or limiting argument has been omitted. This is my own packet closing inspection, not independent Audit A; structural validation is not mathematical certification.\",\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"R001/S001 and F001 export the exact equality between the supplied H and native μH at every positive exponent, the direction of scale monotonicity, and the unbounded-small-scale implication. S002/F002 establish all four critical-exponent implications with their strict ranges. S003 proves inclusion monotonicity and isometric-image invariance from covers, including equality of ambient contents for maps defined only on the set. S004 establishes the two signed power limits and the two exact geometric-series values. The N001 statement includes all these formulas, not just theorem names; no consumer needs R001's body.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"R002/S001 exports boundedness and finite contents for every s,δ>0, with compactness supplying the finite subcovers. S002 constructs the cube grid and proves 0≤D≤n, and separately proves E=V(0), D=0 when n=0 using H002. S003 supplies the actual inverse and squared-distance identity for the concatenation isometry. Each of these clauses appears in N002, including the metric identification used by P.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"R003/S001 obtains the initial cost <ε/2 cover by the scale infimum, with q>0 grounded in N002. S002 supplies an explicit positive-diameter replacement for every singleton and bounds its q-cost by ε2^{-i-2}; the total added budget is at most ε/2. The exported statement quantifies all q>D, 0<r≤1, ε>0 under n≥1, and includes countability, coverage, nonemptiness, the identity r_i=diam(U_i), positive radii, the scale bound and strict total cost <ε.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"R004/S001 handles n=0 by equal interval pieces; S002 derives diam≤√2 r_i and Σ_iN_i(√2 r_i)^{q+1}≤2(√2)^{q+1}Σ_i r_i^q, at r=min(1,δ/√2). S003 closes ε, all scales, and q↓D, with D finite from N002. This proves the unconditional exported inequality dim_H(F)≤D+1 for every ambient case, not merely an estimate at one exponent.\"},{\"id\":\"N005\",\"note\":\"R005/S001 proves the normalization λ(I)=1. S002 proves the nonempty bounded-set guard, α=inf B and β=sup B with β-α≤ρ, and gives the explicit interval J=(α-η/2,β+η/2). It proves containment, the length and measure bounds, and Borel measurability of J and J∩I. These are all exported in N005 so that the slicing and interval-cover consumers can construct J without importing this producer body.\"},{\"id\":\"N006\",\"note\":\"R006/S001-S003 construct the projected covers and Borel majorants without assuming measurability of W_i or their projections, and prove the global indicator inequality. S004 gives c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε with the original η_i and its summable weighted error. S005 first quantifies ε, treats the infinite-cost alternative, then takes the infimum over all covers. Thus N006 is exactly the same-scale inequality for every s>0,δ>0, with no omitted finiteness assumption on the product-cover cost.\"},{\"id\":\"N007\",\"note\":\"R007/S001 uses N006 at every δ and N001 at 0<s<D to obtain H^{s+1}(F)=∞ and dim_H(F)≥s+1. S002 closes the arbitrary s and uses positive finite D from N002 to take its supremum. The exported conclusion retains D>0 as an antecedent; it does not assert this lower bound unconditionally.\"},{\"id\":\"N008\",\"note\":\"R008/S001 proves H^a(I)=0 for every a>1. S002 proves Σ_iρ_i≥1 for every δ-cover by measurable open-interval enclosures and length subadditivity. S003 includes the zero-diameter case in ρ_i^s≥δ^{s-1}ρ_i, then infimizes and sends δ↓0 for 0<s<1. The output explicitly includes H^s_δ(I)≥δ^{s-1}, H^s(I)=∞ and dim_H(I)=1, so the final fibre argument has the exact interval-dimension conclusion.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"R009/S001 combines N004 with N007 when D>0 and, when D=0, uses an H002 witness x_0, the map t↦(x_0,t), N001's isometric-image invariance/monotonicity and N008's dim_H(I)=1. N002 gives exhaustive nonnegative finite D and the Euclidean concatenation identification. Substituting D=dim_H(E) and F=E×I gives the complete spec.conclusion, including n=0 and the exact metric, without joining independent assumptions or weakening the target.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R001/S001-S004 and the actual M001-M005,M012,M013 input statements. S001 proves the native-to-supplied normalization, including removal of the extended scale ∞, enumeration/empty padding and the correct direction under restriction of covers; F001 is universally closed. S002 introduces and discharges the four threshold/measure antecedents under s>0 and then closes positivity, giving the universal F002 without escaped local assumptions. S003 derives inclusion and two-way cover transport under its own L2/L3, using only F001/F002; a positive finite exponent separates unequal extended nonnegative dimensions. S004 uses the two registered power theorems, telescopes finite sums and gives the base/step for 2^m≥m+1, so its geometric-series limits do not need a hidden convergence exchange. Every explicit source has a real role, and no original H is used here.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M001 is instantiated at arbitrary Borel Euclidean X,A,d=s; positive s and finite scale bounds identify native ediam powers with the original costs, and the infinite-scale infimum is bounded by every finite-scale one. M002/M003 use nonnegative s under L6 and exactly L7/L8 as their strict inequalities. M004/M005 use F001 to convert L9/L10 into native zero≠∞ or infinity before delivering their dimension inequalities; no converse is asserted beyond their signatures. M012 is applied at x=0,q=a with a>0 giving its second disjunct, and native 0^a=0 gives the limit. M013 uses the actual negative exponent b<0. All ambient Borel and extended-metric premises are supplied by the fixed Euclidean structures, not by measurability of A.\",\"declaration_check\":\"R001 locals introduce X before A, an arbitrary real s with positivity only in local implications, and the conditional B,Y,φ in S003. F001/F002 have fresh statement-bound X0,A0,p0,d0,r0 and no open assumptions, so they can be instantiated at different sets and exponents. φ is defined only on A and all transported sets are first intersected with A or inverse-imaged into A. The power variables a,b are local to S004; geometric sum indices and natural truncation bounds are bound in those displayed finite identities. No witness, nonempty assumption or bound on A has been smuggled in.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"R002 uses exactly H003, H002 and N001. In S001, compactness is unfolded through D009: integer-radius open balls give boundedness and the radius-δ/2 cover gives finite scale cost. F001 precedes the witness R in S002. For n>0 the displayed grid has at most (2R+1)^n h^{-n} cubes and cost (2R+1)^n n^{a/2}h^{a-n}; a-n>0 grounds the N001 limit. For n=0, only H002 and the V(0) singleton definition are used to identify E. Both branch assumptions and the scale/exponent conditions are closed, giving finite D before later real comparisons. S003's explicit coordinate inverse and squared-distance computation establish the required metric identification without importing an unstated norm equivalence.\",\"source_application_check\":\"There is no direct M/E application. N001 supplies the positive-power limit and zero-measure dimension bounds at exponents a>n>0, or at arbitrary positive exponents in the singleton branch. The application hypotheses are established in the corresponding branches. The use of compactness is a direct application of the supplied finite-open-subcover definition to explicitly displayed open covers, not an omitted substantive compactness theorem.\",\"declaration_check\":\"S001 fixes s,δ only for the finite-content implication; its F002 is closed with fresh p0,d0. R is chosen from the earlier F001, h,a are arbitrary in the n>0 grid, and no singleton witness is needed beyond equality with the empty-tuple space. S003 explicitly introduces x,y∈V(n),t,u∈ℝ for its metric identity. The finite grid coordinate indices are expression-bound, and no grid or branch object escapes into another node.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"R003/S001 uses N002 only for D≥0 and N001 to obtain H^q(E)=0 and zero scale content. The displayed infimum contradiction proves the initial cover existence F001, before W is chosen in S002. Under the complete L1 conditions, singleton replacement is constructed explicitly with diameter min(r/2,(ε2^{-i-3})^{1/q}); its q-cost is strictly below ε2^{-i-2}, and n≥1 provides an actual coordinate direction proving positive diameter. Unchanged members retain their original cost; adding the summable error to the original cost <ε/2 gives the strict final bound <ε. L1 is discharged and all external parameters quantified.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No direct M/E is used. N001 is instantiated at E,q with q>0 proved from N002 and q>D; its geometric-series statement is used with the same original enumeration indices, so discarding empty members cannot increase the replacement-error sum. The native positive-real power identities here have positive bases and q>0, and the minimum is positive and at most r/2; thus no division or root is used outside its domain.\",\"declaration_check\":\"q,r,ε are arbitrary under L1, not original hypotheses. W is a witness from the prior F001; K is the subset of nonempty indices, hence countable. U is given by an explicit formula on its two cases: in the zero-diameter case, nonemptiness and distance separation first prove the unique point exists, then the closed ball is defined. The r_i family is declared as diam(U_i), and all W,K,U,r_i scopes end with the existentially quantified output. No project lemma or additional covering property is hidden in the declarations.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the packet with only N001,N002,N003. S001 uses N002's exported singleton result for n=0 and the supplied equal-piece calculation to prove the entire branch. In S002, L2 is n≥1, L3 is q>D and δ>0, and L4 is the independent ε>0. The N003 cover satisfies all conditions before N_i=ceil(1/r_i) is formed. The partition, countability, Euclidean diameter estimate, ceiling bound N_i≤2/r_i and full cost factor are displayed. S003 discharges/quantifies ε before concluding zero content, then all scales and q>D are closed. D is finite by the direct N002, making q↓D legitimate. No H or producer-body fact is imported.\",\"source_application_check\":\"There is no direct M/E use. N003 is instantiated with r=min(1,δ/√2), which is positive, at most 1 and at most δ/√2; q>D and ε>0 are the local antecedents. N002 gives q>0 because D≥0. N001's zero-measure-to-dimension clause is applied at q+1>0 after every scale content is zero, and its positive-power limit is used at a-1>0 in the zero-ambient case. The final density argument establishes the stated bound even if dim_H(F) was initially infinite.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The singleton branch has its own exponent a and closes without exporting its interval partitions. In the other branch q,δ,ε and r are declared, K,U are direct N003 witnesses, and r_i,N_i are typed local families. K,U,N,r_i end at S002, and F002 exports only their cost consequence, so the S003 ε-limit does not use a cover outside its lifetime. Finite partition indices i,j and truncations are bound by the displayed products and sums.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"R005 uses exactly M009,M010. S001 establishes λ(I)=1. Under the explicit L1 assumptions in S002, a point of B and the finite diameter bound give upper/lower boundedness before infimum and supremum properties are used. For every b∈B, β≤b+ρ shows β-ρ is a lower bound, hence β-α≤ρ. Positivity of η makes the constructed interval contain even unattained endpoints; no assertion that B is measurable is needed. Measure monotonicity supplies the J∩I estimate, and L1 is discharged into the universal statement. Basic real completeness and Borel closure under open/closed sets and intersection are used at their standard hypotheses, with no extra assumptions or substantial new argument.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M010 at endpoints 0,1 gives max(1,0)=1 exactly. M009 is applied at α-η/2 and β+η/2, both finite real numbers after boundedness. The difference is β-α+η>0, so its ofReal/max expression is the stated length. Neither source has an endpoint-order hypothesis, and the simplification is nevertheless grounded by α≤β and η>0. The conclusion λ(J∩I)≤ρ+η follows from actual set inclusion and the delivered measure of J, not from an unsupported assumption that B has length.\",\"declaration_check\":\"B,ρ,η are arbitrary under the complete nonempty/finite-bound/positive-enlargement antecedent. α and β are introduced only after the bounded-nonempty guard is proved in S002, and J is the explicit interval from those reals. Points b used in the order comparisons are quantified over B, not free witnesses escaping the argument. F001 supplies the fixed interval facts without using the enclosure branch.\"},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"R006/S001 uses N002 for finite c and projects an arbitrary δ-cover using the explicit Euclidean squared-distance formula. F001 records all projection/scale guards before N005 is instantiated. S002 keeps arbitrary projections nonmeasurable and uses only enclosing Borel intervals to obtain the pointwise fibre-cover inequality. S003 proves measurability of the actual two-valued functions and the global indicator inequality as F003 before any source requiring it is applied. S004 uses exactly M008,M007,M006,M007, then the original weighted η-error and N001's geometric sum. Comparisons are valid as suprema of finite nonnegative partial sums, including infinite series. S005 quantifies ε before removing it, treats infinite and finite cost separately, and takes the infimum over every cover, closing L3,L2,L1. All direct inputs have actual roles and no integration of a nonmeasurable projection occurs.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M008 at ν=λ compares ind(I,c) with Σ_i f_i; F003 is its exact global pointwise premise. M006 uses X=ℝ,T=ℕ,ν=λ and f_i=ind(J_i∩I,ρ_i^s); countability is explicit, and the earlier F003 establishes measurable and hence almost-everywhere measurable summands. There is no σ-finiteness or finite-integrability condition in its probed signature. M007/A001 on I uses N005's measurable I and λ(I)=1, giving the left integral c. M007/A002 on every J_i∩I uses F002's measurable intersections, giving the exact terms ρ_i^s λ(J_i∩I). N005 is used with nonempty B_i and diam(B_i)≤ρ_i≤δ from F001 and η_i>0; empty W_i are handled separately by empty J_i. Thus every native premise and every bridge to the displayed series estimate is accounted for.\",\"declaration_check\":\"s,δ are arbitrary under L1; W is an arbitrary cover under L2 rather than an assumed globally existing selected cover. c is finite from direct N002, and ρ,A,B are explicitly defined projection/diameter families, with zero conventions for empty members. η has positive denominator 1+ρ_i^s and ε>0. J is the explicit N005 construction with proven nonempty/bounded projection guards, or ∅. f is introduced in S003 only after J and I are Borel. The projection objects stay live through the last use of F001, and J,η,f through S004. In S005 only the cover cost and c survive the ε-quantification; none of the ε-dependent intervals is exported.\"},{\"id\":\"R007\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"The packet has only N001,N002,N006. Under L1:D>0, N002 gives D finite; under L2:0<s<D, N001 gives infinite H^s(E) and small-scale unbounded contents. N006 applies at every δ>0 with s>0; taking the supremum gives H^{s+1}(F)=∞. The critical-exponent clause of N001 gives dim_H(F)≥s+1. S002 closes L2 and takes the supremum over the full nonempty interval 0<s<D; order density and finite positive D give D+1, after which L1 is discharged. This is a conditional derivation, not a new assumption D>0 in the graph.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No direct M/E is used. N006 requires exactly s>0 and δ>0, both explicit in S001. N001's infinite-measure-to-dimension step uses exponent s+1>0. The scale supremum uses the complete N001 and N006 statements, not the producer argument. N002 supplies the finiteness needed when passing s↑D.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The only persistent local is the arbitrary real s under 0<s<D. The scale δ in S001 is universally quantified in the displayed family of inequalities. No scale or large-content witness is selected as a global object; the supremum argument is uniform over all positive scales. L2 and then L1 are closed in their proper order, and the output has no free local parameter.\"},{\"id\":\"R008\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the exact N001,N005,M011 packet. S001 retains m^{1-a}→0 for a>1 and obtains all-scale zero measure before the upper dimension bound. S002 chooses enclosing intervals only for nonempty cover members, with arbitrary ε>0, so countable length subadditivity applies to the majorants rather than arbitrary covering sets. N001's geometric sum yields the original additive ε-error; removing it proves Σ_iρ_i≥1 for every cover. S003 checks positive and zero ρ_i separately, sums the negative-exponent inequality, takes the infimum, then uses the registered negative-power limit through N001. The δ,s limits prove the exact lower bound and dimension one, closing all local cover, tolerance and exponent assumptions.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M011 is instantiated with X=ℝ, the native type of measures on the Borel real line for its FunLike/OuterMeasureClass carrier, ν=λ,T=ℕ,B_i=J_i. λ supplies those measure-evaluation structures and ℕ is countable; no set-measurability premise is invented. N005 applies to W_i with diam(W_i)=ρ_i≤δ finite and η=ε2^{-i-1}>0, and gives λ(J_i)≤ρ_i+η. Empty members get J_i=∅ directly. N001's negative-power limit has exponent s-1<0, while its infinite-Hausdorff-measure implication has positive exponent s. The source conclusions are used with exactly these signs.\",\"declaration_check\":\"a is local to the independent upper calculation. In the lower calculation s,δ,W,ρ remain active through S003, while ε and its explicit interval family J end after the ε-removal in S002. Nonempty-set infimum/supremum guards are available from the direct N005; no missing choice of measurable representative is assumed. Finite interval partitions and sum indices are bound by their displayed formulas, and the exported statement quantifies every exponent and scale rather than leaking W.\"},{\"id\":\"R009\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"R009 uses exactly H002,N001,N002,N004,N007,N008. N002 supplies finite nonnegative D, so D>0 and D=0 are exhaustive. In the positive branch N007 supplies the lower bound under its explicit antecedent. In the zero branch H002 supplies x_0 and the squared-distance formula proves the isometric fibre map; its image lies in F by the definitions of I,F. N001 and N008 then give dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. Both branch assumptions are discharged before combining with N004's upper bound. Finally the exported N002 isometry, not any remembered producer detail, gives the required Euclidean identification. The complete conclusion follows by equality substitution.\",\"source_application_check\":\"There is no direct M/E use. N007 is called only when D>0. N001's isometric-image clause is used for φ:I→V(n)×ℝ with its distance identity explicitly computed and for the N002 concatenation isometry; its inclusion monotonicity is used on φ(I)⊆F. N008 supplies dim_H(I)=1 outright, without reconstructing or importing its proof. Thus all available conclusions and local premises match the actual applications.\",\"declaration_check\":\"x_0 is a branch-local witness whose existence basis is direct H002; no choice is made in the D>0 branch. φ(t)=(x_0,t) is a typed local definition on I, and t,u are universally bound in the distance-preservation verification. Neither x_0 nor φ occurs in the exported P. E,n,I,F,D are the global parameters/definitions with their original domains, and the product-to-Euclidean identification is explicitly supplied by direct N002.\"}] }","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit locat